<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:beh="clr-namespace:Harp.Behavior;assembly=Harp.Behavior"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:dsp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Dsp;assembly=Bonsai.Dsp"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:cv="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Vision;assembly=Bonsai.Vision"
                 xmlns:io="clr-namespace:Bonsai.IO;assembly=Bonsai.System"
                 xmlns:ffm="clr-namespace:Bonsai.FFmpeg;assembly=Bonsai.FFmpeg"
                 xmlns:spk="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Spinnaker;assembly=Bonsai.Spinnaker"
                 xmlns:orc="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:orv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Video;assembly=OpenRigs.Video"
                 xmlns:zmq="clr-namespace:Bonsai.ZeroMQ;assembly=Bonsai.ZeroMQ"
                 xmlns:netmq="clr-namespace:NetMQ;assembly=NetMQ"
                 xmlns:ext="clr-namespace:UclOpenCoenBehaviourBox;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:mf="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Manifest;assembly=OpenRigs.Manifest"
                 xmlns:hd="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.HarpDevices;assembly=OpenRigs.HarpDevices"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Binning" DisplayName="Binning" Description="Camera binning, 1 for full resolution, in place of rig.yml's. Stays set for later runs until cleared. Blank: rig.yml's camera binning." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>RigConfig</Name>
        <Description>Reads &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml once, into the RigConfig subject, then takes out the two devices this workflow drives by name, each into a subject of that name: BehaviorBoard-Main (behaviorBoard: main:) and Camera-Box (camera: box:). Each subject holds the device's Name and its Settings from rig.yml; the name is typed once, in RigDevice, and the device's files take theirs from the subject's Name, so the entry read and the files written cannot disagree. A second camera is another RigDevice and subject, such as Camera-Face. rig.yml is where each name is bound to its hardware (port, serial number); the name is what the data is called. Fails at startup if the machine has no directory or file, or if rig.yml has no entry by either name, saying which entries it has; other entries are ignored. The camera's Binning can be set for one run from this workflow's properties (CameraOverrides); blank keeps rig.yml's. Its ExposureTime and Gain start at rig.yml's and are session parameters, changed live while ready (Hardware &gt; Camera). ExposureFitsTrigger then stops the workflow at Start if rig.yml's exposure, plus 1000 us for the camera, is longer than the board's Trigger0 period (19,000 us at 50 Hz): the camera would skip triggers and every frame would get the wrong time.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="ConfigRoot" DisplayName="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml." />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orc:ResolveRigConfigDirectory">
              <orc:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</orc:ConfigRoot>
            </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Core:ReadRigConfig.bonsai">
              <FileName>rig.yml</FileName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ext:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <ext:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="ext:BehaviourBoxRig" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
              <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
            </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RigConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>BehaviorBoard</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:RigDevice">
                <ext:Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</ext:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Camera</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:RigDevice">
                <ext:Name>Camera-Box</ext:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>Camera-Box</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Binning" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CameraOverrides">
                <ext:Binning xsi:nil="true" />
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:ExposureFitsTrigger">
                <ext:TriggerOutput>0</ext:TriggerOutput>
                <ext:MarginMicroseconds>1000</ext:MarginMicroseconds>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="13" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="11" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The session controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl): SubjectId and SessionId from this node's properties or the command line (--property:SubjectId=...), the run length (whole minutes) and the camera's ExposureTime and Gain (taken live by the camera, Hardware &gt; Camera) as parameters the controller may change until Go, and the control endpoint the rig agent talks to (TCP 5561). The workflow starts into ready mode: board connected, camera armed and streaming, nothing recorded, waiting for Go. At Go the IDs and the run length are checked once and published as RunSettings, which logging waits for; if an ID is empty or the run length is not 1 to 9999, the workflow stops with "Sequence contains no elements." and nothing is recorded. Stop from the controller ends the workflow through ExperimentStoppedException, closing every file.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>RunLengthMins</Name>
                  <Value>30</Value>
                  <Description>How long to record, in whole minutes (1 to 9999).</Description>
                  <Minimum>1</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>9999</Maximum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>ExposureTime</Name>
                  <Value />
                  <Description>Camera exposure in microseconds, taken by the camera live until Go. Starts at rig.yml's; at most the trigger period less 1,000 (19,000 at 50 Hz).</Description>
                  <Minimum>100</Minimum>
                </Parameter>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>Gain</Name>
                  <Value />
                  <Description>Camera gain in dB, 0 to 5, taken by the camera live until Go. Starts at rig.yml's.</Description>
                  <Minimum>0</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>5</Maximum>
                </Parameter>
              </Parameters>
              <Commands />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SubjectId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SessionId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterValue">
                <orcl:Name>RunLengthMins</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Name>RunLengthToInt</scr:Name>
              <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(it)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>RunSettingsValid</Name>
              <Description>Subject and session given, and the run length from 1 to 9999 minutes.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item1.Trim().Length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; Item2.Trim().Length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; Item3 &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; Item3 &lt;= 9999</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:First" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RunSettings</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="9" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The Harp Behavior board (running wheel encoder, camera trigger) and the camera. Each device takes its settings from its own entry in rig.yml, through the subject RigConfig publishes under its name (BehaviorBoard-Main, Camera-Box).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard</Name>
              <Description>Harp Behavior board and the camera trigger on Trigger0 from OpenRigs.Devices, and the running wheel's encoder on port 2 (inline, in Position mode, logged raw). Clock sets the board's clock to UTC when it connects. Triggers start 5 s after RigConfig (at Start, before Go), so the camera is armed first and the preview streams in ready mode.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="PortName" Selector="Settings.PortName" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.BehaviorBoard.bonsai">
                    <CommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</CommandsSubjectName>
                    <PortName>COMx</PortName>
                    <DumpRegisters>true</DumpRegisters>
                    <Heartbeat>Enabled</Heartbeat>
                    <EventsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</EventsSubjectName>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
                    <Name>RunningWheel</Name>
                    <Description>Sets up the running wheel's encoder on port 2 in Position mode, as av-dome does, so the board's AnalogData (register 44) carries the absolute encoder count, logged raw. The OpenRigs.Devices RunningWheel include sets Displacement and then differences and accumulates it, which yields a speed sample rather than a distance; distance is computed offline from the raw count with countsPerRev and wheelDiameterMm in rig.yml.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="beh:CreateMessage">
                          <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                          <harp:Payload xsi:type="beh:CreateEnableEncodersPayload">
                            <beh:EnableEncoders>EncoderPort2</beh:EnableEncoders>
                          </harp:Payload>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="beh:CreateMessage">
                          <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                          <harp:Payload xsi:type="beh:CreateEncoderModePayload">
                            <beh:EncoderMode>Position</beh:EncoderMode>
                          </harp:Payload>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="beh:CreateMessage">
                          <harp:MessageType>Write</harp:MessageType>
                          <harp:Payload xsi:type="beh:CreateEncoderResetPayload">
                            <beh:EncoderReset>EncoderPort2</beh:EncoderReset>
                          </harp:Payload>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
                          <Property Name="Name" DisplayName="CommandsSubjectName" Description="The name of the Subject that carries command messages for a specific behavior device" Category="Subjects" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
                          <Property Name="Name" DisplayName="EventsSubjectName" Description="The name of the Subject that carries event messages from a specific behavior device" Category="Subjects" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
                        </Expression>
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source3" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Trigger0Frequency" Selector="Settings.CameraTriggerController.Trigger0Frequency" />
                      <Property Name="Trigger1Frequency" Selector="Settings.CameraTriggerController.Trigger1Frequency" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.CameraTriggerController.bonsai">
                    <Trigger0Frequency>50</Trigger0Frequency>
                    <Trigger1Frequency>50</Trigger1Frequency>
                    <BehaviorCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BehaviorCommandsSubjectName>
                    <BehaviorEventsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BehaviorEventsSubjectName>
                    <Camera0TriggerEventsSubjectName>Camera0TriggerEvents</Camera0TriggerEventsSubjectName>
                    <Camera1TriggerEventsSubjectName>Camera1TriggerEvents</Camera1TriggerEventsSubjectName>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="BooleanProperty">
                    <Value>true</Value>
                  </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Delay">
                    <rx:DueTime>PT5S</rx:DueTime>
                  </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>StartCameras</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
                    <Name>Clock</Name>
                    <Description>Sets the board's clock to the PC's UTC time (SynchronizeTimestamp, whole seconds) as soon as the board sends its first message, and publishes BoardClockSet once a TimestampSeconds message from the board (its once-a-second heartbeat, or the write's reply) carries a time within 2 s of the PC's UTC time (BoardClockAgrees). Until then each heartbeat that disagrees sends the write again. BoardClockSet does not rely on catching the write's reply: Bonsai subscribes a workflow's branches one after another while the board is already talking, and the branch waiting for the reply could subscribe after it had come (2 Nov 2026: about 1 start in 4 stopped on this Watchdog that way). Without the clock the board counts from power-on, and Harp timestamps, the CSV Seconds column and every file name follow that count (1904-01-04T17-00-00 and so on). The board's own open-time register dump comes before this write and is not logged; Logging waits for BoardClockSet before it logs the board; the dump it keeps is asked for by Logging &gt; RecordHarpDevices, 0.5 s after PathPrefix names the session folder, after Go. If the board's clock does not agree 10 s after Start, Watchdog stops the workflow with a message saying so, rather than record a whole session with no board files; triggers start 5 s after Start, so the session folder then holds a few seconds of video and CSV and no board files. (4 s stopped every run: Watchdog's time counts from the workflow's subscription, before the config and camera are up.)</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                            <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="harp:SynchronizeTimestamp" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="harp:FilterRegister">
                          <harp:FilterType>Include</harp:FilterType>
                          <harp:Register xsi:type="harp:TimestampSeconds" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="harp:FilterMessageType">
                            <harp:FilterType>Exclude</harp:FilterType>
                            <harp:MessageType>Read</harp:MessageType>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                            <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                          <Name>BoardClockSet</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="ext:Watchdog">
                            <ext:DueTime>PT10S</ext:DueTime>
                            <ext:Message>The board did not confirm within 10 s of Start that its clock was set, so nothing from the board is logged. Either its messages are not reaching the PC or the board is not responding. Check the board's USB cable and power (switch it off and on if it is powered), then Start again. The session folder holds a few seconds of video and CSV and no board files.</ext:Message>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="ext:BoardClockAgrees">
                            <ext:Agrees>true</ext:Agrees>
                            <ext:ToleranceSeconds>2</ext:ToleranceSeconds>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="harp:FilterRegister">
                          <harp:FilterType>Include</harp:FilterType>
                          <harp:Register xsi:type="harp:TimestampSeconds" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="harp:FilterMessageType">
                            <harp:FilterType>Include</harp:FilterType>
                            <harp:MessageType>Event</harp:MessageType>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="ext:BoardClockAgrees">
                            <ext:Agrees>false</ext:Agrees>
                            <ext:ToleranceSeconds>2</ext:ToleranceSeconds>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BoardClockSet</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="harp:SynchronizeTimestamp" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</Name>
                        </Expression>
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="6" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="10" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="9" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="14" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>Camera</Name>
              <Description>Frames paired with Harp trigger times. Triggers are Event messages only: the CameraTriggerController subject also carries the register-dump Read reply, which is not a trigger. OpenRigs.Video TriggeredSpinnaker, given the triggers, copies FrameID and Timestamp inside the camera callback, fills FrameID gaps and then pairs frames with triggers, so a dropped frame does not shift later times. Subscribed once rig.yml is read (RigConfig), at Start and before Go, so the preview streams in ready mode; the first frame reports Ready to the controller. Watchdog stops the workflow with a message of its own if no frame arrives for 15 s (usually the trigger cable). The frames are published as Camera-Box.Data, which the live view streams; Value.Image and SampleInterval take 5 images a second from them for the editor's preview window (config\main.layout), from Start, so it shows the camera in ready mode, and the last three nodes show beside it the exposure and gain the camera reports for its frames (CameraSettings). ExposureTime and Gain are session parameters: each starts at Camera-Box's (rig.yml's) value and takes each value the controller sets (OnParameterSet) straight to the open camera, so the preview shows the change while ready; Go fixes them. One second after Start, once the controller's server is up, ParameterDefault shows rig.yml's values as the parameters' values, and ParameterMaximum limits a set exposure to the trigger period less 1000 us, so a longer one is refused at the controller instead of stopping the workflow. Binning is taken only when the camera opens.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Box</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="SerialNumber" Selector="Settings.SerialNumber" />
                      <Property Name="Binning" Selector="Settings.Binning" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="harp:FilterMessageType">
                    <harp:FilterType>Include</harp:FilterType>
                    <harp:MessageType>Event</harp:MessageType>
                  </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="beh:Parse">
                    <harp:Register xsi:type="beh:TimestampedCamera0Frame" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orv:TriggeredSpinnaker">
                    <spk:Index xsi:nil="true" />
                    <spk:SerialNumber />
                    <spk:ColorProcessing>Default</spk:ColorProcessing>
                    <orv:ExposureTime>10000</orv:ExposureTime>
                    <orv:Gain>5</orv:Gain>
                    <orv:Binning>1</orv:Binning>
                  </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="ext:Watchdog">
                      <ext:DueTime>PT15S</ext:DueTime>
                      <ext:Message>No frame from the camera for 15 s, so the run was stopped. Usually the trigger cable from the board's output 0 to the camera; also check the camera's USB cable. Then Start again.</ext:Message>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Box.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Box.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                      <orcl:Phase>Ready</orcl:Phase>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Value.Image</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SampleInterval">
                      <rx:Interval>PT0.2S</rx:Interval>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Box</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Settings.ExposureTime</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnParameterSet">
                      <orcl:Name>ExposureTime</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Convert.ToDouble(it)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="ExposureTime" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Box</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Settings.Gain</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnParameterSet">
                      <orcl:Name>Gain</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Convert.ToDouble(it)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Gain" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Box</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:DelaySubscription">
                      <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1.Settings.ExposureTime</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterDefault">
                      <orcl:Name>ExposureTime</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1.Settings.Gain</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterDefault">
                      <orcl:Name>Gain</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>ExposureLimit</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>The longest exposure that fits the trigger period, less ExposureFitsTrigger's 1000 us margin.</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>1000000.0 / Item2.Settings.CameraTriggerController.Trigger0Frequency - 1000.0</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterMaximum">
                      <orcl:Name>ExposureTime</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Box.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SampleInterval">
                      <rx:Interval>PT0.2S</rx:Interval>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>CameraSettings</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>The exposure and gain the camera reports for its frames (chunk data), 5 a second, for the editor's readout window (config\main.layout): what the camera took, not what was asked for.</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>"Exposure " + Value.ChunkData.ExposureTime.ToString("F0") + " us   Gain " + Value.ChunkData.Gain.ToString("F2") + " dB"</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="16" To="20" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="21" To="5" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="23" To="27" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="26" To="27" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="27" To="28" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="28" To="5" Label="Source4" />
                  <Edge From="29" To="31" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="30" To="31" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="31" To="32" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="32" To="33" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="33" To="34" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="32" To="35" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="35" To="36" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="32" To="37" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="37" To="38" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="39" To="40" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="40" To="41" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges />
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Logging</Name>
        <Description>Waits for RunSettings, then LogController creates the session folder (PathPrefix). Once it exists: the video and its CSV, and, once the board's clock is also set (BoardClockSet, from Hardware > BehaviorBoard > Clock), every Behavior board message, including the register dump RecordHarpDevices asks for once the folder exists, so the board log records the board's settings. The board's own open-time dump, before the clock is set, is not logged. Each device logs into a folder of its own name, taken from its subject's Name (BehaviorBoard-Main, Camera-Box), as &lt;Name&gt;_&lt;DateTime&gt; files in one-hour chunks on the board's Harp clock (the Open Rigs logging spec). Also, once the folder exists, the spec's settings and device metadata: the rig settings as parsed from rig.yml into RigSchema\RigSchema_&lt;DateTime&gt;.json (section 6; the settings at Go are in the manifest's control section), and, from RecordHarpDevices, the board's record BehaviorBoard-Main\BehaviorBoard-Main_device.json and Harp.Behavior's device.yml, the register map, as BehaviorBoard-Main\BehaviorBoard-Main.yml (section 5), so the board's &lt;Name&gt;_&lt;Register&gt;_&lt;DateTime&gt;.bin files can be decoded from the session alone.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RunSettings</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="SubjectId" Selector="Item1.Item1" />
                <Property Name="SessionId" Selector="Item1.Item2" />
                <Property Name="Path" Selector="Item2.RootPath" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogController.bonsai">
              <SubjectId>CHANGE-ME</SubjectId>
              <SessionId>CHANGE-ME</SessionId>
              <Path>C:\Data</Path>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:DelaySubscription">
              <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
            </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RunSettings</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Camera-Box.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>RecordVideo</Name>
              <Description>Subscribed only once PathPrefix exists: Take reads its Count, and the writers may read FileName, at subscription. Records the run length's worth of frames (RunLengthToFrames), split into one-hour chunks on the frames' Harp time (GroupByTime, as the board's log is), each chunk to &lt;Name&gt;\&lt;Name&gt;_&lt;DateTime&gt;.avi and .csv, Name being the camera's from its subject (Camera-Box), named by OpenRigs.Logging's FormatFileName after the chunk's start as the board's files are. CSV columns, as av-dome writes for its cameras: Seconds (Harp time of the frame's trigger), Timestamp and FrameID (camera), ExposureTime. A run crossing the hour gives two pairs; one ffmpeg closes and the next opens there. The video is H.264 through FFmpeg on Intel Quick Sync (Bonsai.Vision's VideoWriter, which av-dome and LogVideo use, fell behind on the N150 and crashed long sessions). ExposureTime is the ExposureTime parameter at Go (rig.yml's unless the controller changed it while ready; fixed from Go), because OpenRigs.Video's frame does not carry the camera's. Wait for ffmpeg.exe to exit before closing Bonsai. SampleInterval here samples the recorded frames, 5 a second; the editor's preview window (config\main.layout) is on Hardware &gt; Camera's last node instead, which takes every camera frame from Start, so it shows the camera in ready mode.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
                    <Name>RunLengthToFrames</Name>
                    <Description>Frames to record: run length (minutes) x 60 x the camera trigger frequency of BehaviorBoard-Main in rig.yml.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>RunSettings</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Name>RunLengthToFrames</scr:Name>
                          <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(Convert.ToDouble(Item1.Item3) * 60.0 * Item2.Settings.CameraTriggerController.Trigger0Frequency)</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Count" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                    <rx:Count>3000</rx:Count>
                  </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orc:GroupByTime">
                      <orc:ChunkSize>1</orc:ChunkSize>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:CreateObservable">
                    <Name>CameraChunk</Name>
                    <Description>One chunk's frames: the video and its CSV, each named after the chunk's start (the group's Key), as OpenRigs.Logging's LogVideo does.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                          <Name>Chunk</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Chunk</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Chunk</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                          <Selector>Key</Selector>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:FormatFileName.bonsai">
                          <Name>UNMAPPED</Name>
                          <Extension>avi</Extension>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="FileName" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="FrameRate" Selector="Settings.CameraTriggerController.Trigger0Frequency" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                          <Selector>Value.Image</Selector>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="ffm:VideoWriter">
                            <ffm:FileName />
                            <ffm:Suffix>None</ffm:Suffix>
                            <ffm:Overwrite>false</ffm:Overwrite>
                            <ffm:FrameRate>50</ffm:FrameRate>
                            <ffm:OutputArguments>-loglevel error -nostats -c:v h264_qsv -preset veryfast -global_quality 20 -bf 0 -pix_fmt nv12</ffm:OutputArguments>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                        <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                          <Selector>Seconds</Selector>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                          <Selector>Value.ChunkData.Timestamp</Selector>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                          <Selector>Value.ChunkData.FrameID</Selector>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterValue">
                            <orcl:Name>ExposureTime</orcl:Name>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Expression>new(
                  Item1.Item1 as Seconds,
                  Item1.Item2 as Timestamp,
                  Item1.Item3 as FrameID,
                  Item2 as ExposureTime)</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Chunk</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                          <Selector>Key</Selector>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:FormatFileName.bonsai">
                          <Name>UNMAPPED</Name>
                          <Extension>csv</Extension>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="FileName" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="io:CsvWriter">
                          <io:FileName />
                          <io:Append>false</io:Append>
                          <io:Overwrite>false</io:Overwrite>
                          <io:Suffix>None</io:Suffix>
                          <io:IncludeHeader>true</io:IncludeHeader>
                          <io:Selector />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Camera-Box</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="Name" Selector="Name" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Camera-Box</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="Name" Selector="Name" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="7" To="11" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="9" To="11" Label="Source3" />
                        <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="13" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="14" To="16" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source3" />
                        <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="16" To="19" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="20" To="25" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="26" To="27" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="27" To="6" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="28" To="29" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="29" To="23" Label="Source2" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Switch" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Value.Image</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SampleInterval">
                    <rx:Interval>PT0.2S</rx:Interval>
                  </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogHarpDevice.bonsai">
              <LogName>UNMAPPED</LogName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="hd:RecordHarpDevices">
              <Name>RecordHarpDevices</Name>
              <Description>Checks the Behavior board at Start and records it into each session, from rig.yml alone (OpenRigs.HarpDevices): for each Harp device in rig.yml whose data this workflow publishes (BehaviorBoard-Main.Data), the board on its portName must have its usbSerial, or the workflow stops saying which board is where; 0.5 s after the session folder (PathPrefix) appears it asks the board for a register dump on BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands, which the board&apos;s log records (Go comes long after BoardClockSet, so the dump is on the UTC clock); and it writes BehaviorBoard-Main\BehaviorBoard-Main_device.json (WhoAmI, hardware, firmware and core versions, Harp and USB serials) and BehaviorBoard-Main\BehaviorBoard-Main.yml, Harp.Behavior&apos;s register map (the Open Rigs logging spec, section 5). A board reporting another WhoAmI stops the workflow. ExperimentManifest expects both files (harp in its ExpectedFiles).</Description>
              <hd:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</hd:ConfigRoot>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="LogName" Selector="Name" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BoardClockSet</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="mf:ExperimentManifest">
              <Name>ExperimentManifest</Name>
              <Description>Writes manifest.json into the session folder (OpenRigs.Manifest), finding PathPrefix itself: once when the folder appears (status partial, outcome running) and again when the run ends. Its input is the run, the frames recorded: completed when the run length&apos;s frames are written, error with a Watchdog&apos;s message, run.items the frame count; a controller stop is stopped, with the stop&apos;s reason. It records the machine, this repo&apos;s commit, Bonsai&apos;s command line (--property values), the settings at Go (SubjectId, SessionId, RunLengthMins), rig.yml&apos;s path and hash as read at Start (its settings are in RigSchema/), and what the session must leave: a folder for each device in rig.yml this workflow publishes (BehaviorBoard-Main/, Camera-Box/), RigSchema/, and (harp) for each Harp device in rig.yml the two files RecordHarpDevices writes, BehaviorBoard-Main_device.json and BehaviorBoard-Main.yml, which the overnight copy (rig-sync) alarms on if missing. A device folder holding only those two counts as empty. Errors on the board&apos;s logging chain do not reach it.</Description>
              <mf:IngestScript>coen-behaviour-box</mf:IngestScript>
              <mf:ConfigFiles>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\rig.yml</mf:ConfigFiles>
              <mf:ExpectedFiles>auto;harp;RigSchema/</mf:ExpectedFiles>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>path</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Recording</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Count" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Finished</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:SessionJson">
                <ext:Name>RigSchema</ext:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:SerializeToJson">
                <ext:Formatting>Indented</ext:Formatting>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="ConfigRoot" />
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="12" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="20" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="15" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="11" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="27" To="31" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="31" To="29" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="28" To="29" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="32" To="16" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every device in this machine's rig.yml that the workflow publishes, over ZeroMQ, for the live view (OpenRigs.LiveView, StreamDevices): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558, on every interface, from Start (in ready mode too). Camera-Box.Data as Camera-Box.video, 5 JPEG frames a second at 320 x 240; BehaviorBoard-Main.Data as BehaviorBoard-Main.encoder, the raw count from AnalogData, 10 a second; each rate and size can be changed in rig.yml under the device's liveView:. Also elapsed, seconds since the session folder (PathPrefix) appeared, once a second, and every 5 s liveview: this workflow, its commit, and the devices streamed and skipped and why. Every message carries RigId, the machine's name, and the session key: "ready" until the session folder exists, then its name, sub-&lt;SubjectId&gt;/ses-&lt;SessionId&gt;_&lt;start&gt;. Its ConfigRoot is the workflow's, as RigConfig's and RecordHarpDevices' are, so --property:ConfigRoot moves all three. Last in the workflow, because it streams only subjects built before it. A port already in use (another workflow streaming) stops the workflow at Start with NetMQ's AddressAlreadyInUseException, before the camera is triggered.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml, read by RigConfig, RecordHarpDevices and LiveView. ExperimentManifest's ConfigFiles names rig.yml's own path and does not follow it; the manifest notes when the two disagree." />
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="1" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="7" To="5" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="6" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
